        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;font color=&quot;#2C3E50&quot; style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;(1)&lt;/b&gt; Formula bar shows =XLOOKUP(B2,SalesOrder!A:A,SalesOrder!D:D), which retrieves the OrderDate from the SalesOrder worksheet by matching on SalesOrderID. Column I uses =IF(C2&amp;lt;H2,&quot;Check&quot;,&quot;OK&quot;) to flag anomalies. &lt;b&gt;(2)&lt;/b&gt; The &quot;Check&quot; result in row 3 flags a record where ShipmentDate (July 1) precedes OrderDate (July 8), indicating a potential accuracy problem.&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
